works and it's  actually a really neat project if you  ask me  uh and then something else i just wanted  to touch on is that you're not going to  know  every answer to their questions you know  and that's okay  they're you know the goal is they're  they're trying to figure out  what what level of knowledge you do have  and so if you don't know the answer to a  question  not a problem don't don't fake it don't  make something up  admit it and speak to how you'd find the  answers so um you know  how would you learn say you don't know  it well what would you do to learn it  you know i would you know i actually i  wouldn't have any problem going home  tonight  and you know signing up for a boot camp  or hopping on some tutorials and just  you know i might just brush up on that  and play with it just to to do that  talk about you can always talk about  previous work history even if it's not  technical  so if you learned something quickly  maybe you were given a task and you  didn't really know  you didn't have that skill set did you  learn something quick did you learn  something on the on the job  um show that you you're willing and  capable of doing that even if it's not  exactly a technical example  so just a little tidbit for junior  developers and  anyone who wants to reach out to me  obviously is welcome to but you know  junior developers i am so  i'm more than happy to talk through  you know anything i can with you to give  you advice you know whatever that looks  like  don't hesitate to reach out to me and  i'll get my contact info here in just a  minute i have a  i think one more slide and then i'll  give you my contact info  so just to conclude uh everything  research do your research that is going  to be  so important for you um you know going  into an interview just  stacked with knowledge the more  information you have the better you're  going to perform  if you're sitting there trying to dig  into your brain and make things up and  it just you're not going to perform well  in an interview so  research come in ready to go read your  job descriptions look at your websites  whatever you need to do linkedin is a  great resource and then practice and  prepare so  for your friends and just go through  even just standard interview questions  you know a lot of interviews you'll get  some standard interview questions so  you know whatever that looks like for  you um you know walk through those and  practice with your friends  and you know be confident so this goes  all the way back to you know earlier  when diana said  don't be afraid to brag about yourself  people don't like doing it  but that's your job in an interview  that's your  sole focus is to sit there and brag  about yourself and to talk about your  experience  and to talk about your accomplishments  um you know you you cannot  you can't not talk about yourself and  brag about yourself and  do very well in an interview so have  some confidence  be proud of yourself be proud of your  accomplishments however  big or small you feel like they are you  know if you're sitting  in that scene in front of a hiring  manager you're in a good spot  so um anyways so that's all i have for  selling yourself one more thing on the  bragging about yourself  um one way that i kind of helped  overcome that a little bit  is instead of thinking about  i'm good at this or i'm good at that i  talk about how proud or excited i was  when i accomplished certain things  and that's one way that you can kind of  redirect that a little bit and still  highlight what you've done  um and talk yourself up without feeling  like  you're bragging about yourself i love  that verbage  you know something that i'm really that  i was really proud of or you can say you  know i did  x y and z and i was really proud of that  i i really like that it does  it does sound um almost better than i'm  really good at this and i'm really good  at that  so i love that  i'll put my contact information up you  can search my name and linkedin  email me that's my direct line if you'd  like to call me  uh don't hesitate to reach out if i can  you know further elaborate on anything  that we talked about today if you need  help with  anything interview-esque um you know i'm  i'm happy to be a resource for  for anyone saying if you have any  questions about tecla home or anything  i'm at diana or at diana barnes  either on taclomaslack or any social  media  so feel free to reach out to me if you  have any questions about anything  okay thank you ashley so much for being  here today we really appreciate this was  a great talk  yeah thank you for having me i loved it


